# Executive Summary
lines.append('<details class="med-details"><summary>')
lines.append("")
lines.append('## Executive Summary</summary><div class="details-content">')
lines.append("")
lines.append("### Major Paradigm Shifts in the 2026 ESC Heart Failure Guidelines")
lines.append("The 2026 ESC Guidelines introduce profound structural and conceptual updates reflecting landmark clinical trials published since 2021:")
lines.append("")
lines.append("1. **Redefined LVEF Phenotypes — Expansion of HFrEF and Abolition of HFmrEF:**")
lines.append("   - **Heart Failure with Reduced Ejection Fraction (HFrEF)** is now expanded to encompass all patients with **LVEF $\\le 50\\%$** (previously $< 40\\%$). Post hoc analyses and dedicated trials demonstrate that patients with LVEF $41\\text{--}49\\%$ derive substantial survival and morbidity benefit from the same foundational neurohormonal therapies as those with LVEF $\\le 40\\%$.")
lines.append("   - **Heart Failure with Mildly Reduced Ejection Fraction (HFmrEF)** has been **officially abolished** as a distinct entity, streamlining clinical decision-making.")
lines.append("   - **Heart Failure with Preserved Ejection Fraction (HFpEF)** is now defined as symptoms/signs of HF with **LVEF $> 50\\%$**, accompanied by objective evidence of elevated filling pressures or structural alterations.")
lines.append("")
lines.append("2. **Adoption of the Universal Stages of Heart Failure (Stages A to D):**")
lines.append("   - **Stage A (At Risk for HF):** Individuals with risk factors (hypertension, diabetes, ASCVD, obesity, cardiotoxic exposure) but no current or prior symptoms, physical signs, or structural/functional cardiac disease or biomarker elevation.")
lines.append("   - **Stage B (Pre-Heart Failure):** Asymptomatic individuals with objective evidence of structural heart disease (e.g., LV hypertrophy, chamber dilatation, wall motion abnormalities, valvular disease), increased filling pressures, or persistently elevated natriuretic peptides / cardiac troponins.")
lines.append("   - **Stage C (Heart Failure):** Patients with current or previous symptoms and signs caused by structural/functional cardiac abnormalities.")
lines.append("   - **Stage D (Advanced Heart Failure):** Patients with severe, refractory symptoms (NYHA class III–IV) despite optimal therapy, frequent hospitalizations, and persistent intolerance to neurohormonal blockers, requiring specialized interventions (LVAD, heart transplantation, palliative inotropes).")
lines.append("")
lines.append("3. **Decompensated Heart Failure (DHF) Replaces \"Acute Heart Failure\":**")
lines.append("   - The term **Decompensated Heart Failure (DHF)** officially supersedes \"acute heart failure\", recognizing that almost all acute presentations represent worsening of an underlying, chronic progressive syndrome rather than isolated acute episodes.")
lines.append("")
lines.append("4. **New Nomenclature for Heart Failure Therapies:**")
lines.append("   - **Foundational Medical Therapy (FMT):** The four core pharmacological pillars (\"quad-therapy\") proven to modify disease trajectory and improve survival: ARNI/ACEi, evidence-based beta-blocker, steroidal MRA, and SGLT2 inhibitor.")
lines.append("   - **Additional Medical Therapy (AMT):** Tailored agents based on specific clinical profiles (vericiguat, ivabradine, GLP-1 receptor agonists, non-steroidal MRAs, digoxin, potassium binders).")
lines.append("   - **Guideline-Directed Device and Interventional Therapy (GDIT):** CRT, ICD, transcatheter edge-to-edge repair (TEER), catheter ablation, and mechanical circulatory support.")
lines.append("")
lines.append("5. **Breakthrough Evidence in Obesity and Cardiometabolic HFpEF:**")
lines.append("   - **GLP-1 receptor agonists (semaglutide, tirzepatide)** are given high-priority recommendations for patients with HFpEF and obesity (BMI $\\ge 30\\text{ kg/m}^2$) based on STEP-HFpEF and SUMMIT trials, demonstrating marked symptom reduction, functional improvement, and reduced HF hospitalization.")
lines.append("")
lines.append("6. **Temporary Mechanical Circulatory Support (tMCS) in Cardiogenic Shock:**")
lines.append("   - Following the **DanGer Shock** trial, routine use of microaxial flow pump (Impella) in selected patients with STEMI-related cardiogenic shock demonstrates reduced 180-day mortality, whereas routine IABP is Class III (no benefit).")
lines.append("")
lines.append("7. **Revolution in Cardiac Amyloidosis (ATTR-CA):**")
lines.append("   - Expanded Class I recommendations for **TTR silencers (vutrisiran)** and **stabilizers (tafamidis, acoramidis)** to reduce cardiovascular hospitalization and all-cause mortality across NYHA classes I–III.")
lines.append("")
lines.append("</div></details>")
lines.append("")

