# Table 6: Revised Recommendations
lines.append('<details class="med-details"><summary>')
lines.append("")
lines.append('### Table 6. Revised Recommendations in the 2026 ESC Heart Failure Guidelines</summary><div class="details-content">')
lines.append("")
lines.append("| Clinical Area | 2021 Recommendation & Class | 2026 Revised Recommendation & Class | Shift & Clinical Rationale |")
lines.append("|---|---|---|---|")
lines.append("| **Hypertension & Stage B (Section 4)** | Treatment of hypertension is recommended to prevent/delay HF (Class I, Level A). | Strict blood pressure control (systolic target $< 130\\text{ mmHg}$) is recommended in patients with hypertension or stage B HF to reduce the risk of HF (**Class I, Level A**). | Specific systolic threshold $< 130\\text{ mmHg}$ mandated to halt progression to stage C. |")
lines.append("| **CMR in Aetiology (Section 5)** | CMR recommended with poor echo window (Class I, Level C). | Contrast-enhanced CMR is recommended in suspected cardiomyopathy or uncertain aetiology if further characterization adds value (**Class I, Level C**). | Direct tissue characterization with LGE indicated early in diagnostic pathway. |")
lines.append("| **Invasive Coronary Angiography (Section 5)** | Recommended in angina or ventricular arrhythmias (Class I, Level B). | Recommended in HF, angina, and high probability of obstructive CAD who are potential candidates for revascularization (**Class I, Level C**). | Aligned with REVIVED-BCIS2 findings focusing revascularization on symptom relief. |")
lines.append("| **MRA Across LVEF Spectrum (Section 6)** | MRA recommended for HFrEF (Class I, Level A); may be considered in HFmrEF (Class IIb, Level C). | An MRA (steroidal for HFrEF; steroidal or non-steroidal for HFpEF) is recommended in symptomatic HF independent of LVEF (**Class I, Level A**). | Universal Class I indication for MRA across the entire ejection fraction spectrum. |")
lines.append("| **Cardiac Glycosides (Section 6)** | Digoxin may be considered in HFrEF in sinus rhythm (Class IIb, Level B). | Digoxin or digitoxin should be considered in symptomatic HFrEF with LVEF $\\le 40\\%$, despite optimal FMT, to reduce HFH (**Class IIa, Level B1**). | Upgraded to Class IIa based on DIG trial long-term re-analyses and DIGIT-HF trial data. |")
lines.append("| **Vericiguat (Section 6)** | May be considered in NYHA II–IV with worsening HFrEF (Class IIb, Level B). | Vericiguat may be considered in symptomatic HFrEF with LVEF $< 45\\%$ despite optimal FMT to reduce HFH and CV death (**Class IIb, Level B1**). | Clarified LVEF cutoff $< 45\\%$ post-worsening event. |")
lines.append("| **CRT in AV Block (Section 6)** | CRT recommended rather than RV pacing in high-degree AV block (Class I, Level A). | CRT rather than RV pacing should be considered in HFrEF regardless of QRS width with pacing indication for high-degree AV block (**Class IIa, Level B1**). | Refined evidence base differentiating conduction pacing from biventricular pacing. |")
lines.append("| **Decongestion with Diuretic Combinations (Section 7)** | Thiazide combination should be considered in resistant oedema (Class IIa, Level B). | Addition of short-term IV acetazolamide or oral hydrochlorothiazide should be considered in fluid overload to reduce congestion (**Class IIa, Level B1**). | Supported by ADVOR (acetazolamide) and CLOROTIC (HCTZ) randomized trials. |")
lines.append("| **IABP in Cardiogenic Shock (Section 7)** | IABP not routinely recommended in post-MI cardiogenic shock (Class III, Level B). | IABP is not recommended in unselected patients with cardiogenic shock due to lack of effect (**Class III, Level B1**). | Broadened Class III across all unselected cardiogenic shock etiologies. |")
lines.append("| **Temporary MCS (Section 7)** | Short-term MCS considered as BTR, BTD, BTB (Class IIa, Level C). | Temporary MCS should be considered in selected patients with HF-related haemodynamic instability as BTR, BTD, BTB, BTC, or BTT (**Class IIa, Level C**). | Inclusion of Bridge-to-Candidacy (BTC) and Bridge-to-Transplant (BTT). |")
lines.append("| **Continuous Inotropes in Advanced HF (Section 8)** | May be considered as bridge to MCS/transplant (Class IIb, Level C). | Continuous inotropes should be considered in advanced HFrEF, low cardiac output, and hypoperfusion as BTD, BTT, or bridge to durable MCS (**Class IIa, Level C**). | Upgraded to Class IIa for structured bridge pathways. |")
lines.append("| **Durable MCS / LVAD (Section 8)** | Long-term MCS should be considered as BTT or destination therapy (Class IIa, Level A/B). | Durable MCS (LVAD) is recommended in selected patients with advanced HFrEF despite FMT and GDIT, as BTT, BTC, BTR, or destination therapy (**Class I, Level C**). | Upgraded to Class I recommendation for eligible end-stage patients. |")
lines.append("| **Beta-Blockers in AF Rate Control (Section 9)** | Should be considered for short- and long-term rate control (Class IIa, Level B). | Beta-blockers are recommended in stable patients with HFrEF and AF as first-line therapy for rate control (**Class I, Level C**). | Upgraded to first-line Class I for rate control in stable HFrEF. |")
lines.append("| **Catheter Ablation for AF in HFrEF (Section 9)** | Should be considered if clear association with symptom worsening (Class IIa, Level B). | Catheter ablation for AF should be considered in selected patients with symptomatic AF and HFrEF to improve QoL and reduce HFH or death (**Class IIa, Level C**). | Consolidated role for early pulmonary vein isolation in HF patients. |")
lines.append("| **Coronary Revascularization in CCS (Section 9)** | Should be considered for persistent angina (Class IIa, Level C). | Coronary revascularization is recommended in patients with HF, obstructive CAD, and persistent angina despite FMT and antianginal drugs (**Class I, Level C**). | Upgraded to Class I specifically for symptom relief in refractory angina. |")
lines.append("| **Aortic Stenosis Interventions (Section 9)** | TAVI or SAVR recommended in severe high-gradient AS (Class I, Level B). | Aortic valve intervention, SAVR or TAVI, is recommended in patients with severe aortic stenosis and HF to improve symptoms and reduce death (**Class I, Level B1**). | Re-emphasized Class I indication regardless of low-flow/low-gradient subtype. |")
lines.append("| **Mitral TEER in Secondary MR (Section 9)** | Should be considered in carefully selected patients (Class IIa, Level B). | Mitral transcatheter edge-to-edge repair is recommended in stable symptomatic HFrEF with persistent severe secondary MR despite FMT/CRT meeting criteria (**Class I, Level B1**). | Upgraded to Class I based on COAPT trial long-term 5-year outcomes. |")
lines.append("| **Remote PA Pressure Monitoring (Section 11)** | May be considered in symptomatic HF (Class IIb, Level B). | Remote haemodynamic monitoring of PA pressure should be considered in symptomatic HF, NYHA class III and prior HFH in past 12 months (**Class IIa, Level B1**). | Upgraded to Class IIa based on CHAMPION and MONITOR-HF trial data. |")
lines.append("| **Transthyretin Amyloidosis (Section 12)** | Tafamidis recommended in hTTR-CA and wtTTR-CA NYHA I–II (Class I, Level B). | Treatment with TTR silencer (vutrisiran) or stabilizer (tafamidis, acoramidis) is recommended in variant or wild-type ATTR-CA across NYHA I–III (**Class I, Level A**). | Upgraded to Class I, Level A; includes gene silencers (vutrisiran) and novel stabilizers. |")
lines.append("")
lines.append("</div></details>")
lines.append("")

